#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# jacobi_epsilon

#% text
# `jacobi_epsilon(u, m)` gives the Jacobi epsilon function `E(am(u | m) | m)`, the integral of `jacobi_dn(t, m)^2` for `t` from 0 to `u`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 22.16.14. `jacobi_epsilon(K(m), m)` is `E(m)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
jacobi_epsilon(0.5, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.48062514580838267

#% cell
jacobi_epsilon(1.0, 0.9)
#% output
#= 0.7823869783816086

#% cell
jacobi_epsilon(elliptic_k(0.5), 0.5) - elliptic_e(0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral of `dn^2`:

#% cell
n_integrate(jacobi_dn(t, 0.4)^2, [t, 0, 0.7]) - jacobi_epsilon(0.7, 0.4)
#% output
#= 2.220446049250313e-16

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `jacobi_zn`, `elliptic_e`, `jacobi_dn`
